---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const seo = {
  title: "Income Tax Calculator FY 2025-26 Comparison: Old vs New Regime | Arthavi",
  description: "Detailed comparison of Old vs New Tax Regime for FY 2025-26. Learn how new tax slabs, standard deductions, and surcharges impact your salary net take-home.",
};
---
<Layout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  keywords="income tax calculator 2025-26 comparison, old vs new tax regime 2025 26, income tax slabs FY 2025-26, new regime slabs AY 2026-27, tax saving calculator India"
  schema={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BlogPosting",
    "headline": "Income Tax Calculator FY 2025-26 Comparison: Old vs New Regime",
    "image": "https://arthavi.com/images/og-image.png",
    "author": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Arthavi"
    },
    "publisher": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Arthavi",
      "logo": "https://arthavi.com/images/logo.png"
    },
    "datePublished": "2026-07-24",
    "dateModified": "2026-07-24"
  })}
  breadcrumb={{
    items: [
      { name: "Home", url: "https://arthavi.com/" },
      { name: "Blog", url: "https://arthavi.com/blog/income-tax-calculator-2025-26-comparison" }
    ]
  }}
>
  <main class="container" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem);">
    <article class="prose fade-in" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; color: var(--text-body); line-height: 1.8;">
      <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-head);">Income Tax Calculator FY 2025-26 Comparison: Old vs New Regime</h1>

      <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        Are you trying to decide between the Old and New Tax Regimes for Financial Year (FY) 2025-26 (Assessment Year 2026-27)? Recent revisions have made the new tax regime highly attractive for the majority of salaried individuals.
      </p>

      <p>In this analysis, we perform an in-depth <strong>income tax calculator 2025-26 comparison</strong> to see which tax regime saves you more money based on your annual deductions and salary slabs.</p>

      <h2>New Tax Regime Slabs (FY 2025-26)</h2>
      <p>Under the new tax regime, tax rates are lower, and standard deduction is set to ₹75,000 for salaried employees. The tax slabs are structured as follows:</p>
      <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
        <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1.5rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem;">
          <thead>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1); text-align: left;">
              <th style="padding: 0.75rem;">Income Slab</th>
              <th style="padding: 0.75rem;">Tax Rate (New Regime)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Up to ₹3,00,000</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-head);">Nil</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">₹3,00,001 to ₹7,00,000</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-head);">5%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">₹7,00,001 to ₹10,00,000</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-head);">10%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">₹10,00,01 to ₹12,00,000</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-head);">15%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">₹12,00,01 to ₹15,00,000</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-head);">20%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Above ₹15,00,000</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-head);">30%</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Importantly, Section 87A rebate makes net taxable incomes up to ₹7,00,000 completely tax-free under the new regime.</p>

      <h2>Old Tax Regime Slabs (FY 2025-26)</h2>
      <p>The old tax regime retains standard deductions (₹50,000) and allows various exemptions (HRA, LTA, Section 80C, Section 80D, Section 24b). Slabs remain unchanged:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Up to ₹2.5 lakh: Nil</li>
        <li>₹2.5 lakh to ₹5 lakh: 5%</li>
        <li>₹5 lakh to ₹10 lakh: 20%</li>
        <li>Above ₹10 lakh: 30%</li>
      </ul>

      <div style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2rem; background: var(--bg-surface); border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
        <h2 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--text-head);">The Break-Even Deduction Rule</h2>
        <p>To determine if the old regime is better, find your <strong>break-even deduction point</strong>. If your total deductions exceed the break-even threshold, the old regime is better; otherwise, choose the new regime.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>For an income of <strong>₹10,000,000</strong>, the break-even deductions are approximately <strong>₹2,50,000</strong>.</li>
          <li>For an income of <strong>₹15,000,000</strong>, the break-even deductions are approximately <strong>₹3,75,000</strong>.</li>
          <li>For an income of <strong>₹20,000,000</strong>, the break-even deductions are approximately <strong>₹4,25,000</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Common deductions to reach these thresholds include: Section 80C (₹1.5L), Section 24b Home Loan Interest (₹2L), Section 80D Health Insurance (₹25K–75K), and HRA exemption.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="glass-panel" style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--primary-glow); border-radius: 12px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.01);">
        <h2 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--primary-glow);">Calculate Your Best Regime Instantly</h2>
        <p>Don't calculate slab distributions and break-even points manually. Arthavi has created a premium, ad-free Income Tax Regime Comparison calculator for FY 2025-26.</p>
        <p>Input your salary and deductions to see your old vs new regime liability side-by-side, complete with marginal relief calculations.</p>
        <div style="margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center;">
          <a href="/income-tax-calculator/" class="btn" style="background: var(--primary-glow); color: #fff; padding: 0.75rem 2rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold; display: inline-block;">Compare Regimes Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Conclusion</h2>
      <p>Unless you have high deductions (like home loan interest + high basic HRA + ELSS + NPS), the new tax regime will save you both money and tax compliance effort. Use <a href="/income-tax-calculator/" style="color: var(--primary-glow); text-decoration: underline;">Arthavi's Free Income Tax Calculator</a> to compare your exact tax liabilities today.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
